# DO wine.keep-thread-handles
#
# For an Allegro 4.x Windows game that sometimes hangs as it exits: its log
# stops at "Exiting Allegro" (or its own last shutdown line), its window stays
# up, it uses no CPU, and it happens on some exits and some Macs more than
# others. Allegro's timer waits without limit on a thread's handle that the C
# runtime closed when the thread ended, and Wine may have given that value
# to something else by then. This keeps the handle of every thread
# `_beginthread` starts open, in this stage's own Wine (its 32-bit
# msvcrt.dll), so the wait sees the thread has ended. Put it after the stage
# has Wine (FROM --module=wine… prefix); a game without it gets Wine as it
# comes. docs/modules.md#the-wine-modules-patches has the details.
FUNCTION keep-thread-handles
  WINE.KEEP-THREAD-HANDLES
END
